  "notes": "Southern Dagaare orthography uses 'ky' and 'gy' for the affricates [t͡ʃ] and [d͡ʒ], and 'kp', 'gb', 'ŋm', 'ny' for co-articulated or palatal consonants. Nasalization is marked with a tilde on the vowel. Long vowels are written as double vowels and are treated as sequences of two phonemes. The language has a 9-vowel system with ATR harmony, but the orthography uses 7 vowel letters, meaning 'i' and 'u' may represent both +ATR and -ATR variants. Nasalisation is handled by the combining tilde in \"diacritics\"; precomposed nasal vowels are therefore not listed as separate graphemes.",
